# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env — BUILD-TIME environment for `cargo build` / `cargo run`.
#
# These values are read at COMPILE TIME and baked into the binary.
# Changing them requires a rebuild.
#
# Cargo automatically loads variables from this file when you run
# `cargo build` / `cargo run` from the workspace root (via
# rust-toolchain / cargo-env-file integration, or by sourcing this
# file yourself: `set -a && . ./.env && set +a`).
#
# DO NOT put runtime secrets here — those go in `.env.user`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED — the auth-server URL baked into the binary as the trust
# anchor. There is intentionally NO default; the build fails if this
# is unset. Refusing a default prevents shipping a binary that silently
# points at the wrong auth backend.
#
# Production:
AUTH_URL=https://auth.vexarr.com
